From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:52:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 110/159] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7250-motorola-nairo: Use 25 mA
 per WLED string

Downstream uses 25 mA on PM8150L v2.0 and later; this PMIC is v3.0.

These changes were written with the help of an LLM and checked by a human.

Assisted-by: LLM dtschema
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RmfiVDW3KWZdb9c3iDGRYg
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts
index d438c64f4ff2..6845c11b1be3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250-motorola-nairo.dts
@@ -523,11 +523,11 @@ &pm8150l_lcdb_ncp {
 &pm8150l_wled {
 	/*
 	 * Values from the downstream DT: four strings (string-cfg 0xf), 20.5 V
-	 * OVP, 1050 mA boost limit. Downstream uses 25 mA per string, or 20 mA
-	 * on PM8150L v1.0; use the lower value until the revision is known.
+	 * OVP, 1050 mA boost limit. Downstream uses 25 mA per string on
+	 * PM8150L v2.0 and later (this one is v3.0), 20 mA on v1.0.
 	 */
 	qcom,current-boost-limit = <1050>;
-	qcom,current-limit-microamp = <20000>;
+	qcom,current-limit-microamp = <25000>;
 	qcom,ovp-millivolt = <20500>;
 	qcom,num-strings = <4>;
 
